    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (6 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe business-day rule already rolled weekends forward but ignored public holidays. I extended it in the one place that owns the definition of \"business day.\"\n\n**`BusinessDays.java`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 added the fixed holiday calendar and made the roll-forward skip holidays as well as weekends:\n- New `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` constant: `2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28`.\n- Extracted a single `isBusinessDay(date)` predicate (not Sat, not Sun, not a holiday) and rewrote `rollForward` to advance one day until it hits a business day. This naturally chains past runs of weekend + holiday.\n\nThe pipeline (`RollRegistrationDateToBusinessDay`, `EnsureDailyLimit`, and `owners.POST.yml`) needed no changes \u2014 they already delegate to `BusinessDays.rollForward`, so both the new-owner default date and the daily-limit count now respect holidays automatically.\n\n**`BusinessDaysTest.java`** (new unit test, same package to reach the package-private helper) covers:\n- plain weekday unchanged,\n- weekend \u2192 Monday,\n- weekday holidays (Thu 01-01 \u2192 Fri 01-02; Mon 01-26 \u2192 Tue 01-27),\n- a holiday that also falls on a weekend (Sat 04-25 \u2192 Mon 04-27),\n- the consecutive-obstacle chain (Fri 12-25 holiday \u2192 weekend \u2192 Mon 12-28 holiday \u2192 Tue 12-29).\n\nThe existing `AcceptanceTest` (weekend invariant on the default date) still passes.",
